# Drift-clarification state

The previous turn flagged a preference contradiction and asked the oracle to clarify.
The oracle's current message is their response to that clarification question.

Your task here is narrow: decide whether the contradiction was real or not.

- **drift_confirmed** — the oracle's reply shows they genuinely changed their preference
  (e.g. "yes I changed my mind", "actually I want that now", "ignore what I said before").
  Use this when the oracle reaffirms the new, contradicting preference.
- **drift_dismissed** — the oracle's reply explains the contradiction away
  (e.g. "no I meant something else", "you misunderstood", "I was describing what I don't want").
  Use this when the oracle is NOT actually changing the earlier stated preference.

Do NOT emit **clarify_drift** again — one clarification is enough. Commit to confirmed or
dismissed based on the oracle's reply. You may still emit **natural_end** if the oracle
signals they are done with the conversation. Emit **proceed** only if the reply is entirely
ambiguous (cannot determine confirmed or dismissed).

